+### Ollama setup on this Windows PC
+
+When the selected Gateway advertises an Ollama setup action, choose **Set up**
+on its Ollama card. Companion checks the selected Gateway and this PC separately.
+It does not treat an empty model list or a failed connection as proof that an app
+is not installed.
+
+1. If the Gateway already finds an Ollama model, **Use detected model** continues
+   through the existing exact-model activation and verification flow. The review
+   displays the detected model before you choose it. No Windows app installation
+   or launch is needed.
+2. For a verified installed app that is not active, **Open Ollama** opens that app
+   without reinstalling it. An active app or service is never launched again by
+   this action. Unknown or conflicting installation/activity facts show details
+   and **Check again**, not a guessed install action.
+3. If no supported installation registration or active service is found, review
+   **Install and open Ollama**. The native review names the version, app storage
+   requirement, package license and Microsoft WinGet source information. Check
+   the download/installation consent before continuing. Acquisition is pinned to
+   the reviewed official package and requires matching hash and trusted Ollama
+   publisher verification before execution. It does not run a downloaded script,
+   repair trust policy or replace an existing installation. If a llama.cpp server
+   is present, installation is blocked: the upstream installer can terminate
+   `llama-server.exe`, including unrelated runtimes. Stop it through its existing
+   owner before installing; Companion never stops it for you. Keep other local
+   model servers stopped until installation finishes.
+4. App installation does not include a model or finish AI setup. A reachable app
+   without a usable local chat model remains **needs model**. Choose one in
+   Ollama, then **Check again**, or use **Connection setup** to enter the existing
+   Gateway-owned provider workflow. Model downloads require their own explicit
+   confirmation there; app consent does not authorize them.
+5. A Windows-side response does not prove that a native isolated, WSL or remote
+   Gateway can reach the same service. **Connection setup** retains that selected
+   Gateway's address/auth/model ownership. Companion does not change firewall,
+   proxy, WSL networking, app credentials or Ollama sharing permissions.
+
+Before installer admission, **Cancel** stops that action. After admission,
+**Cancel further setup** withdraws subsequent steps but waits for Windows
+installation to settle. Companion does not terminate the installer's launched
+app, uninstall partial/existing installations, delete models or automatically
+retry an uncertain outcome. Closing setup or quitting Companion retains the
+admitted operation and its log until cleanup finishes, before releasing the
+setup lock. A hung installer remains pending rather than being declared safely
+cancelled; inspect Windows installation state before a fresh reviewed retry.
+
+The external Ollama app keeps its own settings, model cache and lifetime. This
+flow adds no Windows node/MCP command and does not enable inference sharing.
+Llama.app, Companion-managed llama.cpp and model acquisition are separate owners.
+
 ### Llama.app local model setup
 
 Llama.app is the preferred **fresh** local-model handoff. Companion recommends
